<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banda Aceh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kutaraja</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Banda <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> is a port city at the northern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, near the entrance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-malacca">Strait of Malacca</a>. As the capital of the Aceh Sultanate from the sixteenth century it dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a> trade, and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rule after 1874 it was called Kutaraja. Nearby lay the earlier harbour kingdom of Lamuri. The city was devastated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> tsunami of 2004.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banda-aceh.jpg" alt="Banda Aceh" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Si Gam · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meuseujid_Raya_Baiturrahman,_Aceh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
